[Music]  this is one of the biggest humanitarian  aid operations in the world  at the u.n syria cross border aid center  in turkey's hatai province  freight trucks are loaded with critical  aid including food  medical supplies and shelter materials  but this may be one of their last  shipments to northern syria  what you see behind me is the last  delivery from the u.n to the north of  syria  through the years we've tried to provide  better conditions for the displaced  civilians  and lift their standards of living by  providing aid if this aid stops we will  return to zero  trucks have carried critical aid into  the region since 2014.  most of the four million people in  syria's northwest  including the 2.6 million internally  displaced  depend on humanitarian aid delivered  through the only u.n authorized border  crossing  babel hawa the aid is vital for millions  of people devastated by a decade of war  if we don't receive the aid we aren't  able to survive  can anyone survive without water and  food i lost my husband in the war and  i'm looking after seven kids  aid groups say last year the u.n funded  204 humanitarian programs  in northwest syria worth 300 million  dollars  if the cross-border aid mechanism is not  relieved  90 million dollars of funding could be  lost  but syrian president bashar al-assad's  main ally russia  is indicating it won't work to relieve  the program  after it expires on july 10.  moscow says the u.n aid should be  delivered to assad's government  in damascus  [Music]  the regime will use the aid as a weapon  against people in northern syria  if it's distributed through damascus  we've seen the regime act that way in  the past  and we demand the international  community will act  duan says some of syria's most  vulnerable people live in  italy province and the failure to extend  authorization for the delivery of aid to  them  will have devastating consequences  millions of people are scattered across  hundreds of similar camps  with 